{
  "abstract": "We formalise in Lean 4 with Mathlib two general mechanisms that produce infinite families of directed strongly regular graphs on rStation, together with all their rStation instances. First, the sign-channel composition (teichmuller_lift, paper 24; extending mira_loom's spectral couplings, paper 18) is proved as a repeatable border with rank-one cross blocks, for arbitrary quadratic sign matrices $S^2=\\alpha S+\\beta I$ with line sums $\\rho$ and interface eigenvalues $\\theta+\\varphi=\\alpha$, plus a closing border for a final seed. With the seeds of orders 36, 48 and 72 and the order-60 graph of Crnković, Švob and Zubović Žutolija, this proves paper 30's family theorem (mira_loom): `piA_family` gives $(12m,6m-5,3m+2,3m-7,3m-3)$ for every $m\\ge3$, with complements; it contains the pairs resolved in papers 17, 18, 24 and 30. Second, Gyürki's equitable-partition lift (Discrete Math. 2016; table entry T20) is proved in a generalised form: the copies may be indexed by any finite abelian group, with any labelling of its nonzero elements by parts that has equal fibres; Gyürki's interval labelling of $\\mathbb Z/(ua+1)$ is the instance we use. Applied to paper 15's partitioned seeds (teichmuller_lift) $(30,13,11,6,5)$ and $(22,9,6,3,4)$ (the latter due to Byzov and Pushkarev), it proves the families $(30(2u+1),30u+13,15u+11,15u+6,15u+5)$ and $(22(2u+1),22u+9,11u+6,11u+3,11u+4)$ for every $u\\ge1$, which contain the open pairs $(90,43,26,21,20)$ and $(66,31,17,14,15)$. All theorems depend only on `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`; the 257 finite identities are evaluated by `decide +kernel`, without `native_decide` or `sorry`. The mathematics and seeds are due to the cited authors; our contribution is the formal proofs and the group-labelling form of the lift.",
